Unicode combining characters should be handled correctly by par. For
example, É can be represented as E followed by a combining acute accent
(U+0301). Similarly, è can be written as e followed by combining grave
accent (U+0300).

When reformatting text, par should count these as single visual units,
not as two separate characters. This is important for proper line
breaking and width calculation.

Test cases include: café, naïve, Zürich, and résumé.
